WEBVTT

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:05.810
There are two options for transferring
stitches from the ribber to the main bed.

00:00:05.843 --> 00:00:07.850
You can also use this the other way.

00:00:07.883 --> 00:00:12.290
From the main bed down to the ribber
using a double eyed needle.

00:00:12.323 --> 00:00:18.080
First take the stitch off
onto that double eyed needle.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.090
Flip the needle and slide
the stitch to the other end.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:27.650
Then position the opening of the double
eyed needle over the hook of the main

00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:31.170
bed needle and slip off the stitch.

00:00:31.203 --> 00:00:33.690
Now this looks harder than it is.

00:00:33.723 --> 00:00:39.170
Once you get a feel for it and establish
a rhythm, it goes pretty quickly.

00:00:39.203 --> 00:00:43.690
If you're like me and your double eyed
needle likes to play hide and seek,

00:00:43.723 --> 00:00:47.250
try using two transfer tools.

00:00:47.283 --> 00:00:51.880
From the top, slip the ribber stitch
to the transfer tool and put

00:00:51.913 --> 00:00:54.610
the ribber needle out of work.

00:00:54.643 --> 00:01:00.490
From the bottom, insert a second transfer
tool into the stitch and transfer

00:01:00.683 --> 00:01:03.770
that stitch to the new tool.

00:01:03.803 --> 00:01:08.010
Put the eye of that second tool over
the main bed needle and slip

00:01:08.043 --> 00:01:12.120
the stitch to the main bed needle.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:18.290
Again, this looks harder than it is
and you may prefer this method even if you

00:01:18.323 --> 00:01:20.640
can find that pesky double eyed needle.

